{"id": 10, "ts": 1780631071.665139, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and rapid decision\u2011making, and James\u2019s confirmation that C \u201cunderstands complicated technology\u201d and processes information quickly. Those are indeed strong technical and cognitive indicators. However, the long\u2011distance pilot role also demands proven stress resilience and the ability to manage complex, variable operational environments such as weather forecasting. My notes show that Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress very well, and is good at assessing weather conditions\u2014critical for international routes where rapid adaptation to changing meteorology is essential. While B\u2019s pretentious demeanor and occasional tone issues raise crew\u2011cooperation concerns, they appear less severe than C\u2019s egocentric attitude and reluctance to pursue further education, which could limit ongoing learning and feedback orientation. Given the balance of stress resilience, technical aptitude, and the need for continuous development on long\u2011haul flights, I would provisionally recommend **Candidate\u202fB** as the stronger overall fit."}
